      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pomfret%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s Air Line Trail follows a former railroad bed linking Pomfret to Putnam, offering scenic seven‑mile rides through the Bafflin Sanctuary.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pomfret%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Pomfret Historical Society, founded in 1976, preserves landmarks like the 1841 Old Town House and the 1890 Brayton Grist Mill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        3,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://pomfret-historical-society.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ernest Flagg designed Pomfret School, a college‑prep campus built in 1894, sharing his work with the U.S. Naval Academy and New York’s Singer Building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pomfret%2C_Connecticut"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Renée Zellweger bought a 1770 farm in Pomfret in 2004, adding a touch of Hollywood to the town’s historic landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
